<title>USA: Clinton to float extending capital gains exclusion.</title>
<headline>Clinton to float extending capital gains exclusion.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton plans on Thursday to propose extending the home sellers capital gains tax exemption, White House aide Gene Sperling told reporters.</p>
<p>Under current law, people over the age of 55 can claim a one-time tax exclusion of $125,000 on the sale of a home.</p>
<p>Sperling said Clinton's proposal would eliminate the age limit and would increase the tax exclusion to $250,000 for a single person or $500,000 for a couple filing their income taxes jointly.</p>
</text>
